<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><subtitle type="html">Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/rss</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:56:16Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Israel kills six in Gaza hospital strike as 9-month-old baby freezes to death</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:db4a16c1e0fd1a251e17c7eef1f550243438e5b298e5f6ac80e81b0649ee3deb</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:55:12Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T16:18:24Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261112-israel-kills-six-in-gaza-hospital-strike-as-9-month-old-baby-freezes-to-death--43c83484c699.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261112-israel-kills-six-in-gaza-hospital-strike-as-9-month-old-baby-freezes-to-death" /><summary type="html">An overnight Israeli air strike on Nasser Hospital in southern Gaza killed at least six Palestinians Thursday, including a teenage boy and a surgeon, medics said. Elsewhere in the devastated Palestinian territory, a nine-month-old baby died from the cold as families flee worsening flooding.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>How FRANCE 24 traced Tehran-backed Afghan fighters from Syria to southeastern Iran</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:91dd0e2764c56cdb8eda2065b747f4e73d896cdc8d346ab38f97ed024ccd339b</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:54:12Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T16:03:26Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261112-iran-afghan-fatemiyoun-fighters-syria-baluchistan" /><summary type="html">Members of the Tehran-backed Afghan Shia militia known as the Fatemiyoun division have resurfaced in Iran after largely disappearing from public view following the fall of Bashar al-Assad’s government in Syria in 2024. FRANCE 24 used "martyrdom” announcements and the geolocation of videos shared on social media to trace their presence.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>At least five people shot in DC neighbourhood near the White House</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:20fb760cdb26cf9838febfe7c5a533153af906d94f70f5625df623e7941543ab</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:55:18Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T16:01:57Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261112-at-least-five-people-shot-in-dc-neighbourhood-near-the-white-house--c1ab95e70108.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261112-at-least-five-people-shot-in-dc-neighbourhood-near-the-white-house" /><summary type="html">At least one person died after five people were shot early Thursday in a Washington, DC neighbourhood near the White House, police said. A swarm of officers responded to a nearby apartment building where a suspect was barricaded and later shot himself.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Life through a lens: Celebrating 200 years of photography</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4930307cb5f6f2daa88e65f7f5b0c7ed1ab7e1be9b3d72d5f8591d6d11752784</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:55:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T15:56:15Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/arts24/20261112-life-through-a-lens-celebrating-200-years-of-photography--90c03e83bbea.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/arts24/20261112-life-through-a-lens-celebrating-200-years-of-photography" /><summary type="html">A passport photo, a selfie, an award-winning film and even the evening news: all of them were made possible thanks to a "fantastic machine", the camera. As France celebrates the bicentenary of the first fixed photographic image, we discuss the image-obsessed society we live in with filmmaker Maximilien Van Aertryck and artist Alina Frieske.</summary><category term="arts24" /></entry><entry><title>US Defence Secretary Pete Hegseth reprimanded at war memorial</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fc5958605091ff2bf8decbf287d8b78bad9e12254ab76834a48197252ce2620d</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:55:24Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T15:51:49Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/us-defense-secretary-pete-hegseth-reprimanded-at-war-memorial--332f267ab309.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/us-defense-secretary-pete-hegseth-reprimanded-at-war-memorial" /><summary type="html">US Defence Secretary Pete Hegseth, along with his wife and aides, was silenced by a guard on Wednesday at the Tomb of the Unknown Soldier. Hegseth's group was at Arlington National Cemetery for a Veterans Day ceremony when they were reprimanded for laughing and taking pictures in front of the sombre memorial.</summary></entry><entry><title>Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang resigns after revelations on extramarital affairs</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:07d911b0ff40dbb4ad0a7b0232e025fb660329684b5e71a8cc2256092bf63b8f</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:55:27Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T15:46:08Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261112-nvidia-ceo-jensen-huang-resigns-after-revelations-on-extramarital-affairs--11a6bfe4bbc3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261112-nvidia-ceo-jensen-huang-resigns-after-revelations-on-extramarital-affairs" /><summary type="html">Jensen Huang resigned as chief executive of AI giant Nvidia on Thursday, November 12, after revelations he had two extramarital affairs, including one with a woman accused of spying for China. FRANCE 24's correspondent in Washington Fraser Jackson and FRANCE 24's International Affairs Commentator Douglas Herbert have more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang steps down</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:80ab6bd7c4ed7f1e798472cfa2640d0b079144cb9e8b175c8b8de4c28f4b76fe</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:55:30Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T15:45:53Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261112-nvidia-ceo-jensen-huang-steps-down--459853504274.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261112-nvidia-ceo-jensen-huang-steps-down" /><summary type="html">Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang resigned Thursday after his extramarital affair raised national security concerns, in a spectacular downfall for the longtime head of the chipmaker, a vital player in the artificial intelligence boom. The scandal has sent shares of the multi-trillion-dollar company plunging, and the exit of Huang, who has been a key promoter of the artificial intelligence boom, leaves Nvidia without its leather-jacket-clad leader at a crucial time for the sector.</summary></entry><entry><title>European security and Ukraine talks top agenda at Dublin summit</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:840adc64b00a2e45121afa7e0628ab6996a5987d59d4675d1b0dfd4ca36c7ecc</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:55:33Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T15:44:56Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261112-european-security-and-ukraine-talks-top-agenda-at-dublin-summit--5cbdc3de5c87.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261112-european-security-and-ukraine-talks-top-agenda-at-dublin-summit" /><summary type="html">Leaders from more than 50 European countries and institutions are gathering in Dublin for the European Political Community summit, hosted by Ireland under the theme “Europe – strong, secure and connected”. The summit highlighted the need for Europe to have a seat at the table in any discussions shaping its future, amid an ongoing debate over how the continent should respond to US-led efforts to negotiate an end to the war in Ukraine with Russia. FRANCE 24's Europe Editor Armen Georgian tells us more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Australia: Teen found alive after six days missing in bush</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:68b44196928abca2f8cb94bd5ccbb8faec0f069dad3bc9e8e4da9f6ba7a52f01</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:55:36Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T15:17:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261112-australia-teen-found-alive-after-six-days-missing-in-bush--8db19d8790e6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261112-australia-teen-found-alive-after-six-days-missing-in-bush" /><summary type="html">A 17-year-old Australian has been found alive and well after spending six days missing in bushland east of Melbourne. After being spotted by helicopter, the teen was winched to safety before an emotional reunion with his mother who joked that “he’s never leaving the house again”.</summary></entry><entry><title>For the love of French butter: 'Le beurre' spreading joy globally</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6e1782d9caa3a079000f93ec19ac0d3a4489d1ad6c1c0aca27e2cbdef31e8284</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:55:39Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T14:56:01Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/entre-nous/20261112-for-the-love-of-french-butter-le-beurre-spreading-joy-globally--c736d76eb81b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/entre-nous/20261112-for-the-love-of-french-butter-le-beurre-spreading-joy-globally" /><summary type="html">French butter is having a moment! We dive into France's love of butter, the many rules that apply to "le beurre", how tourists are hauling back flavoured artisan butter as souvenirs, and how the French language has embraced many a butter expression over the years.</summary><category term="Entre Nous" /></entry><entry><title>Armed robbers flee Paris De Beers store on motorcycles after jewellery heist</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4abef02305cd1fc21b237de1acceeb533cc97a722c8d447669c4d80e036ebbcb</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:55:42Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T14:42:43Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france/20261112-armed-robbers-flee-paris-de-beers-store-on-motorcycles-after-jewellery-heist--ce90a7416e3e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261112-armed-robbers-flee-paris-de-beers-store-on-motorcycles-after-jewellery-heist" /><summary type="html">Four black-clad individuals sped away from De Beers jeweller in Paris's second arrondissement Thursday morning after stealing hundreds of thousands of euros worth of luxury goods at gunpoint. Police are searching for those responsible.</summary><category term="France" /></entry><entry><title>ICRC 'currently classifying the highest number of armed conflicts since the Second World War</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:114c7462847a4559c6c5f28e9099775f2b402f840ffc40b362cfcd135c1fc208</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:55:45Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T14:33:19Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261112-icrc-we-are-currently-classifying-the-highest-number-of-armed-conflicts-since-the-second-wo--30b88dd630a4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261112-icrc-we-are-currently-classifying-the-highest-number-of-armed-conflicts-since-the-second-world-war" /><summary type="html">François Picard is pleased to welcome the President of the International Committee of the Red Cross, Mirjana Spoljaric. “You may consider war a human condition,” argues Spoljaric. “But brutality, barbarity, is not a human condition.” Her warning recalls the fundamental premise of the 1949 Geneva Conventions: even in war, there can be no lawless space, and certain red lines must never be crossed.</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>France's social safety net: Can it afford to be so generous?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a217a6e578feb0e0910b2c494001c56c39717d3673c54c00cc83d817f86de58b</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:55:48Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T14:28:11Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/french-connections/20261112-france-s-social-safety-net-can-it-afford-to-be-so-generous--3ebba1302ba7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/french-connections/20261112-france-s-social-safety-net-can-it-afford-to-be-so-generous" /><summary type="html">Created in the aftermath of World War II, France's social security system has become one of the pillars of French society, providing everything from healthcare and family benefits to pensions. But with an ageing population and mounting deficits, this ambitious model is facing a major financial test. We look at how the system works, why it is so deeply valued by the French and whether the country can afford to keep its promise of protecting everyone – from cradle to grave.</summary><category term="French connections" /></entry><entry><title>ICRC 'currently classifying the highest number of armed conflicts since the Second World War'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c0977854117963340426d64d8c075e742681fc0a365ede380820ef4bb2778398</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:55:51Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T14:23:33Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261112-icrc-we-are-currently-classifying-the-highest-number-of-armed-conflicts-since-the-second-wo--42213c89e973.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261112-icrc-we-are-currently-classifying-the-highest-number-of-armed-conflicts-since-the-second-world-war" /><summary type="html">François Picard is pleased to welcome the President of the International Committee of the Red Cross, Mirjana Spoljaric. “You may consider war a human condition,” argues Spoljaric. “But brutality, barbarity, is not a human condition.” Her warning recalls the fundamental premise of the 1949 Geneva Conventions: even in war, there can be no lawless space, and certain red lines must never be crossed. Spoljaric warns that the international rules established to protect civilians are being progressively weakened amid proliferating armed conflicts, technological transformations and the retreat of diplomacy.</summary></entry><entry><title>Mississippi elects its first African American to US Senate since Reconstruction</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:43b4374f83c03cf9e519efe8459865765025a4f53ca8a157a71d782047a438b1</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:55:55Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T14:23:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261112-mississippi-elects-its-first-african-american-to-us-senate-since-reconstruction--c58f82d3f782.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261112-mississippi-elects-its-first-african-american-to-us-senate-since-reconstruction" /><summary type="html">Democrat Scott Colom defeated Republican Senator Cindy Hyde-Smith to become Mississippi’s first Black US Senator since Reconstruction. His narrow victory, confirmed on November 11 after prolonged ballot counting, marks a major political shift in the conservative state. FRANCE 24's International Affairs Commentator Douglas Herbert has more.</summary></entry><entry><title>France: Five men on trial for murder of anti-drug activist Amine Kessaci's brother</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8c5324212e87ff3665c5eea4a4f9330c6994b113200038fbc87418e7d08f621f</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:55:57Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T14:20:36Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261112-france-five-men-on-trial-for-murder-of-anti-drug-activist-amine-kessaci-s-brother--97c5322846e1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261112-france-five-men-on-trial-for-murder-of-anti-drug-activist-amine-kessaci-s-brother" /><summary type="html">In France, the trial of five men accused of murdering the brother of anti-drug activist Amine Kessaci is under way. Amine Kessaci, originally known as an environmental activist, became a prominent figure in the fight against drug-related crime after losing two of his brothers to violence linked to drug trafficking. The defendants face the possibility of life imprisonment. The verdict is expected on Monday, November 16. FRANCE 24's International Affairs Editor Angela Diffley tells us more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Huang powers and bankrolls AI revolution: Nvidia CEO caught between 'a rock and a very hard place'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0b623da313436f4ad1266e7791b56d1b983b612f1e3573e9ac6be3d397365033</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:56:01Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T14:11:34Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261112-he-powers-and-bankrolls-ai-revolution-nvidia-ceo-huang-caught-between-rock-and-a-very-hard---ce288d10e4d5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261112-he-powers-and-bankrolls-ai-revolution-nvidia-ceo-huang-caught-between-rock-and-a-very-hard-place-1" /><summary type="html">Oliver Farry is pleased to welcome Bernard Benhamou, Secretary General of France's Institute of Digital Sovereignty. Benhamou examines the intersection of traditional espionage, geopolitical rivalry and the extraordinary concentration of power within the global AI industry. Discussing allegations surrounding Nvidia's leadership, he describes the chipmaker as "the banker of the global AI system," a striking characterization that captures the company's importance not merely as a semiconductor manufacturer, but as a central actor in the economic and technological infrastructure underpinning the AI boom. "Because humans stay humans." Benhamou identifies one of the central paradoxes of the artificial intelligence revolution: even as technological systems acquire unprecedented strategic and economic importance, the individuals who control them remain susceptible to familiar forms of influence, manipulation and misjudgment.</summary></entry><entry><title>🔴 Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang to step down after affair</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b072bd9b7277f0368c336427884918a9e3c9c9fdd538290381b445c3b9f8e80d</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:56:03Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T14:07:56Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261112-nvidia-ceo-jensen-huang-to-step-down-after-affair--76e88ca56800.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261112-nvidia-ceo-jensen-huang-to-step-down-after-affair" /></entry><entry><title>Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang resigns after affair raises national security concerns</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:58b265a205b1fc2ad1db5e46c68ce0c4b18f85ccb1750fd57084b65884fbd625</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:56:03Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T14:06:37Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261112-nvidia-ceo-jensen-huang-to-step-down-after-affair--76e88ca56800.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261112-nvidia-ceo-jensen-huang-to-step-down-after-affair" /><summary type="html">Nvidia announced on Thursday that CEO Jensen Huang was stepping down following revelations that he had an affair with a woman accused of spying for China. The company's chief financial officer Colette Kress will serve as interim CEO while the board searches for Huang's successor.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>Can the fight against climate change be good for business?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0111ce1974738a8e3903271587fa9f182352d607dc1404467005cac872245b29</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:56:07Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T13:59:03Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/people-profit/20261112-can-the-fight-against-climate-change-be-good-for-business--87d29dc6cf25.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/people-profit/20261112-can-the-fight-against-climate-change-be-good-for-business" /><summary type="html">Industries across the globe are seeking to reduce their carbon footprint and become more sustainable. To do so, many are turning to employees with specific credentials. According to LinkedIn's Global Green Skills Report 2026, workers with green skills are being hired at more than 1.5 times the rate of the wider workforce.</summary><category term="People &amp; Profit" /></entry><entry><title>Midterms: Democrat Colom claims historic win in Mississippi</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:60a7cedc7c908c14f388cc615311317a9e5bdd872c05ba65c7fc7a5045dd087b</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:56:09Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T13:37:11Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261112-midterms-democrat-colom-claims-historic-win-in-mississippi--0cb079298e3c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261112-midterms-democrat-colom-claims-historic-win-in-mississippi" /><summary type="html">Scott Colom has become the first Black person to win a Senate race in Mississippi since 1874 and the first Democrat to do so since 1982 after being declared the victor in a razor-edge election on Wednesday. The win is a stunning upset in one of the country’s most reliably red states, adding to what were already sweeping gains by the Democrats at the midterms.</summary></entry><entry><title>War photographer Patrick Chauvel: 'People have lost faith in the press'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:40c23bd4d4fc94da5b1923e963ea14ff78c298fa9f3c47a0c53130503409bf41</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:56:13Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T13:33:46Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/perspective/20261112-war-photographer-patrick-chauvel-people-have-lost-faith-in-the-press--43447068b061.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/perspective/20261112-war-photographer-patrick-chauvel-people-have-lost-faith-in-the-press" /><summary type="html">One of France's top war photographers, who has a 50-year CV of taking pictures in and around conflicts across the planet, has spoken to FRANCE 24 about his concerns that people have lost faith in the press. He notes that journalists are only looking for the truth. Patrick Chauvel has produced nearly 380,000 photographs, from Vietnam to Cambodia, from Afghanistan to Palestine, from Lebanon to Ukraine. He says he wants to take people by the hand to show them how the press works and why.</summary><category term="Perspective" /></entry><entry><title>🔴Live: Putin offers to evacuate civilians from eastern Ukraine's Kostiantynivka</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:70b2d4817b730d3ff78e724d8d45367744a2d8b1d7531e0cc9d018b16fb1b001</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:54:12Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T13:02:30Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261112-live-us-envoys-to-meet-putin-and-zelensky-after-abu-dhabi-talks--eb0f36381594.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261112-live-us-envoys-to-meet-putin-and-zelensky-after-abu-dhabi-talks" /></entry><entry><title>Israeli occupation in southern Lebanon: Displaced families struggle to cope</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7e219981997bda543086dc6aea98040c1e231acb374f4a2b4504d4431d1cd59a</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:56:16Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T11:51:05Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261112-israeli-occupation-in-southern-lebanon-displaced-families-struggle-to-cope--b0f3878e931e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261112-israeli-occupation-in-southern-lebanon-displaced-families-struggle-to-cope" /><summary type="html">In Lebanon, more than 360,000 people are still displaced after months of war between Israel and Hezbollah, according to the UN. Along the border, the Israeli army claims to be fighting the Iran-backed militant group but now occupies 6 percent of Lebanese territory and is wiping entire villages off the map. In the border area, we meet families living in makeshift housing. Many fear they may never go home.</summary><category term="Focus" /></entry></feed>
